# Python (ai-pipeline/)
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.venv/
venv/

# Node (viewer/)
node_modules/
dist/

# Copied engine WASM build output (regenerated via npm run sync-engine-wasm,
# sourced from the gitignored engine/build_wasm/)
viewer/src/shell/public/engine/

# Copied demo CT series (regenerated via npm run sync-demo-ct, sourced from
# the Git LFS-tracked test-data/lidc_idri/) -- gitignored here rather than
# committed a second time, to avoid double-storing ~68MB of LFS data (same
# reasoning as public/engine/ above).
viewer/src/shell/public/demo-ct/

# Playwright output
viewer/test-results/
viewer/playwright-report/
viewer/src/workers/inference-worker/test-results/
viewer/src/workers/inference-worker/playwright-report/

# PID file for scripts/dev-server.ps1's background npm run dev tracking
viewer/.dev-server.pid

# Generated model artifacts — not committed, regenerated via convert_to_onnx.py / quantize_ptq.py
*.onnx
*.onnx.data
# Exception: a tiny (190-byte), checked-in dummy model for e2e plumbing
# tests -- not a real/raw generated model artifact, see its own
# generate-dummy-onnx.py for what it actually is. Duplicated (not
# symlinked/synced) into public/models/ so the real Shell UI's "Load Demo
# Model" button can actually fetch it in a browser -- tests/fixtures/ is
# not on any servable path, unlike public/, which is why the copy exists
# instead of pointing the UI at the same file the generator writes to.
!viewer/tests/fixtures/dummy-lungmask.onnx
!viewer/src/shell/public/models/dummy-lungmask.onnx

# Exception: the real quantized lungmask model (REQ-A02 INT8 output),
# checked in so the Shell's "Load Segmentation Model" button has something
# real to fetch in a browser -- REQ-A06's integration criterion (§5.3.1)
# specifically requires the real 2.5D lung model, not the dummy above.
# Copied from ai-pipeline/quantization/ rather than symlinked, same
# portability reasoning as the dummy model's own copy.
!viewer/src/shell/public/models/lungmask_r231_int8.onnx

# Exception: the FP16 variant of the same model (Issue #35) -- the
# Inference Worker now picks INT8 or FP16 at runtime based on whether a
# WebGPU adapter is available (see worker.ts's modelBasePath handling and
# docs/verification/inference-worker.md §8.4: FP16 is fastest on WebGPU,
# INT8 is fastest on WASM but the slowest of the three on WebGPU), so both
# variants need to be fetchable, not just INT8.
!viewer/src/shell/public/models/lungmask_r231_fp16.onnx

# Calibration/sample CT data (e.g. LIDC-IDRI) — never commit raw medical imaging data.
# dir/* (not a bare dir/) so the exceptions below can carve out a minimal,
# attributed CI/test fixture subset from inference_fixtures/ and
# ground_truth_fixtures/ -- ai-pipeline/quantization/README.md documents
# both directories and this exception in full.
ai-pipeline/quantization/calibration_data/*

# Exception: a minimal, curated subset (the same 5 of ~30 locally-generated
# slices in both directories below) that inference-worker's vitest/Playwright
# suites need and a fresh CI checkout otherwise can't run against. Tracked via
# Git LFS (.gitattributes), same "never commit raw medical imaging data,
# except one deliberately attributed subset" pattern as test-data/lidc_idri/
# below. Everything else in each locally-regenerated pool stays gitignored.
!ai-pipeline/quantization/calibration_data/inference_fixtures/
ai-pipeline/quantization/calibration_data/inference_fixtures/*
!ai-pipeline/quantization/calibration_data/inference_fixtures/manifest.json
